WEBVTT

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:02.971
Last video, we put one function inside another.

00:00:03.413 --> 00:00:04.661
Now let's multiply two of them.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.789
Here's e to the x, here's sine x,

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.994
and here's their product, e to the x

00:00:10.155 --> 00:00:10.595
sine x.

00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:13.771
A quick guess for its derivative: just multiply

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:14.495
the two derivatives.

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:17.068
That gives e to the x times cos

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:17.168
x.

00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:20.323
At pi over two, cos x is zero,

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:22.291
so the guess says the curve is flat

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:22.512
there.

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:24.045
But look at the curve.

00:00:24.548 --> 00:00:26.615
At pi over two, it's climbing steeply.

00:00:27.198 --> 00:00:30.036
So how do both factors really contribute to

00:00:30.057 --> 00:00:30.438
the slope?

00:00:31.076 --> 00:00:31.901
Here's a way to see it.

00:00:32.525 --> 00:00:34.311
Think of the product as the area of

00:00:34.352 --> 00:00:36.578
a rectangle, with width e to the x

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.224
and height sine x.

00:00:38.988 --> 00:00:41.236
At x equals one, it's about two point

00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:43.827
seven two wide, and point eight four high.

00:00:44.452 --> 00:00:45.805
Now nudge x a little.

00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:48.539
The width grows, and that adds a strip

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.010
down the side: the change in width, times

00:00:51.031 --> 00:00:51.371
the height.

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:53.982
The height grows too, adding a strip along

00:00:54.003 --> 00:00:56.172
the top: the change in height, times the

00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:56.393
width.

00:00:57.116 --> 00:00:59.440
The corner is a small change times a

00:00:59.461 --> 00:01:01.805
small change, so it vanishes as the nudge

00:01:01.846 --> 00:01:02.166
shrinks.

00:01:03.049 --> 00:01:05.093
So the area changes in two ways,

00:01:05.775 --> 00:01:07.559
one factor changing while the other stays.

00:01:08.241 --> 00:01:10.165
Divide by the nudge, and that's the product

00:01:10.206 --> 00:01:11.046
rule from Year 11:

00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:13.792
u prime v, plus u v prime.

00:01:14.495 --> 00:01:15.237
Back to the curve,

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.862
at x equals one.

00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:19.469
E to the x's turn is its slope

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.834
times the height of sine x, about two

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:22.516
point two nine.

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:25.385
Sine's turn is the height of e to

00:01:25.446 --> 00:01:27.392
the x times sine's slope,

00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:29.077
about one point four seven.

00:01:29.921 --> 00:01:32.875
Together that's about three point seven six, the

00:01:32.896 --> 00:01:33.759
slope of the tangent.

00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:36.321
Now slide to pi over two.

00:01:37.026 --> 00:01:38.431
Sine x is at the top of its

00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:40.780
hump, so its slope is zero, and its

00:01:40.861 --> 00:01:41.824
turn is zero.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.371
But e to the x is still growing,

00:01:44.773 --> 00:01:46.617
and sine x is still one high,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.043
so e to the x's turn gives the

00:01:49.145 --> 00:01:51.390
whole slope, about four point eight one.

00:01:52.173 --> 00:01:54.485
The guess multiplied a slope by a slope,

00:01:54.828 --> 00:01:55.471
so it missed this.

00:01:56.129 --> 00:01:56.713
Keep sliding.

00:01:57.358 --> 00:01:59.999
Past pi over two, sine x starts to

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.840
fall, so its slope is negative,

00:02:02.401 --> 00:02:04.901
and its turn pulls the slope down, while

00:02:04.922 --> 00:02:06.922
e to the x's turn still pushes it

00:02:07.024 --> 00:02:07.123
up.

00:02:08.025 --> 00:02:10.231
At three pi over four, the two turns

00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:13.181
are equal and opposite, about plus and minus

00:02:13.302 --> 00:02:14.465
seven point four six.

00:02:15.169 --> 00:02:17.368
They cancel, so the tangent is flat.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.914
That's why this curve levels off at three

00:02:19.955 --> 00:02:22.299
pi over four, not at pi over two,

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.822
where sine x levels off.

00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:26.495
E to the x is still growing, and

00:02:26.556 --> 00:02:28.084
it carries the product further.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:29.795
Now the algebra.

00:02:30.339 --> 00:02:32.926
Differentiate y equals e to the x sine

00:02:33.048 --> 00:02:33.167
x.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.801
Label the factors first.

00:02:35.611 --> 00:02:37.181
u is e to the x, so u

00:02:37.242 --> 00:02:38.469
prime is e to the x.

00:02:38.973 --> 00:02:41.501
v is sine x, so v prime is

00:02:41.562 --> 00:02:41.943
cos x.

00:02:42.646 --> 00:02:44.953
Then u prime v, plus u v prime,

00:02:45.316 --> 00:02:47.442
gives e to the x sine x, plus

00:02:47.604 --> 00:02:48.827
e to the x cos x.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.573
Both terms share e to the x, so

00:02:51.614 --> 00:02:52.534
take it out as a factor:

00:02:53.096 --> 00:02:55.019
e to the x, times sine x plus

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:55.360
cos x.

00:02:56.165 --> 00:02:56.998
Check pi over two.

00:02:57.424 --> 00:02:59.310
That's e to the pi over two, times

00:02:59.532 --> 00:03:01.981
one plus zero, about four point eight one,

00:03:02.403 --> 00:03:03.025
the slope we saw.

00:03:03.677 --> 00:03:05.151
The same rule works with a log.

00:03:05.656 --> 00:03:08.462
Differentiate y equals e to the x, times

00:03:08.503 --> 00:03:09.544
the natural log of x.

00:03:10.307 --> 00:03:12.932
The natural log needs x positive, so this

00:03:12.994 --> 00:03:15.839
function only exists for x greater than zero.

00:03:16.684 --> 00:03:18.432
u is e to the x, and so

00:03:18.554 --> 00:03:19.176
is u prime.

00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:22.067
v is the natural log of x, so

00:03:22.128 --> 00:03:23.892
v prime is one over x.

00:03:24.555 --> 00:03:26.282
That gives e to the x times the

00:03:26.323 --> 00:03:28.051
natural log of x, plus e to the

00:03:28.192 --> 00:03:28.854
x over x.

00:03:29.618 --> 00:03:31.220
Take out e to the x, and you

00:03:31.261 --> 00:03:33.083
get e to the x, times the natural

00:03:33.124 --> 00:03:35.247
log of x plus one over x, for

00:03:35.309 --> 00:03:35.949
positive x.

00:03:36.772 --> 00:03:38.559
Every new family works the same way:

00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:41.192
two turns, then look for a common factor.

00:03:41.862 --> 00:03:44.358
Next, a factor with a function inside.

00:03:44.881 --> 00:03:48.081
Differentiate y equals x cubed, sine two x.

00:03:48.805 --> 00:03:51.759
The outside operation is multiplication, so it's the

00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:52.301
product rule.

00:03:53.306 --> 00:03:55.639
u is x cubed, so u prime is

00:03:55.699 --> 00:03:56.544
three x squared.

00:03:57.288 --> 00:04:00.006
Now check v before you write its derivative.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.993
Sine two x has an inside, two x,

00:04:03.415 --> 00:04:05.157
so by the chain rule from last video,

00:04:05.499 --> 00:04:07.481
v prime is two cos two x.

00:04:08.304 --> 00:04:08.503
Then

00:04:09.026 --> 00:04:11.352
u prime v, plus u v prime, is

00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:14.220
three x squared sine two x, plus two

00:04:14.321 --> 00:04:15.825
x cubed cos two x.

00:04:16.566 --> 00:04:18.890
Both terms share x squared, so the answer

00:04:19.011 --> 00:04:21.395
is x squared, times three sine two x,

00:04:21.536 --> 00:04:23.178
plus two x cos two x.

00:04:23.989 --> 00:04:25.235
Does that two matter?

00:04:25.941 --> 00:04:27.754
Check the slope at pi over two.

00:04:28.581 --> 00:04:31.536
There, sine pi is zero, and cos pi

00:04:31.678 --> 00:04:32.502
is minus one.

00:04:33.163 --> 00:04:35.364
So the first term vanishes, and the slope

00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:38.126
is two, times pi over two cubed, times

00:04:38.247 --> 00:04:38.847
minus one.

00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:41.713
That's minus pi cubed over four,

00:04:42.235 --> 00:04:44.118
about minus seven point seven five,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.921
and the tangent agrees.

00:04:46.705 --> 00:04:48.754
Leave out the two, and you'd get half

00:04:48.815 --> 00:04:51.064
of that, a tangent that's far too shallow.

00:04:51.678 --> 00:04:52.674
Here's a way to remember it.

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:55.310
Each factor takes a turn, and the other

00:04:55.412 --> 00:04:55.954
one stays.

00:04:56.698 --> 00:04:58.882
In the rectangle, the width changes while the

00:04:58.943 --> 00:05:01.609
height stays, then the height changes while the

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.210
width stays.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.043
That's why there are two terms, and why

00:05:05.144 --> 00:05:07.514
each term keeps one of the original factors.

00:05:08.358 --> 00:05:11.165
Multiplying the two derivatives keeps neither factor, so

00:05:11.186 --> 00:05:12.008
it isn't the rule.

00:05:12.772 --> 00:05:14.660
And because the two turns are added, it

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.187
doesn't matter which factor you call u.

00:05:17.153 --> 00:05:18.528
That won't be true for a quotient.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:21.598
Your turn.

00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:24.758
Differentiate f of x equals x squared e

00:05:24.799 --> 00:05:26.826
to the x, and give your answer fully

00:05:26.867 --> 00:05:27.409
factorised.

00:05:27.932 --> 00:05:28.717
Pause here to answer.

00:05:40.282 --> 00:05:42.897
u is x squared, so u prime is

00:05:42.997 --> 00:05:43.460
two x.

00:05:44.204 --> 00:05:46.190
v is e to the x, and so

00:05:46.271 --> 00:05:46.913
is v prime.

00:05:47.735 --> 00:05:49.677
So f prime of x is two x

00:05:49.817 --> 00:05:51.899
e to the x, plus x squared e

00:05:51.959 --> 00:05:52.359
to the x.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.342
Both terms share x e to the x,

00:05:55.802 --> 00:05:57.603
so f prime of x is x e

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.585
to the x, times x plus two.

00:06:00.507 --> 00:06:02.913
Multiplying the derivatives gives just two x e

00:06:02.933 --> 00:06:05.179
to the x, which loses the second turn.

00:06:06.944 --> 00:06:07.348
Last one.

00:06:08.153 --> 00:06:10.841
Find the exact gradient of the curve y

00:06:10.982 --> 00:06:13.229
equals x e to the minus x,

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:14.994
at x equals two.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.593
Pause here to answer.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.005
u is x, so u prime is one.

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:32.873
v is e to the minus x, which

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:35.779
has an inside, minus x, so v prime

00:06:36.041 --> 00:06:37.943
is minus e to the minus x.

00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:40.870
So d y by d x factors to

00:06:41.352 --> 00:06:43.756
e to the minus x, times one minus

00:06:43.898 --> 00:06:43.997
x.

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:47.444
At x equals two, that's minus e to

00:06:47.465 --> 00:06:48.166
the minus two,

00:06:48.668 --> 00:06:50.191
about minus point one three.

00:06:50.973 --> 00:06:52.978
Lose the minus from the inside, and you'd

00:06:52.999 --> 00:06:54.803
get a positive slope, but the curve is

00:06:54.864 --> 00:06:55.445
falling there.

00:06:57.115 --> 00:06:59.200
So in a product, each factor takes a

00:06:59.241 --> 00:07:00.765
turn, while the other one stays.

00:07:01.709 --> 00:07:03.819
Next, one function divided by another.

00:07:04.544 --> 00:07:06.492
Here's e to the x, over x plus

00:07:06.614 --> 00:07:06.753
one.

00:07:07.418 --> 00:07:08.993
There's a gap where the bottom is zero.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.171
So how does dividing change the slope?

00:07:14.855 --> 00:07:15.738
Here are the key notes.

00:07:16.261 --> 00:07:18.029
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:18.531
to copy them.
